On 31 March 2026 the cash book of Bello Enterprises showed a debit bank balance of ₦86,000. When the cash book was compared with the bank statement the following were discovered:
(i) cheques issued to suppliers but not yet presented to the bank, ₦24,000;
(ii) cheques received and lodged but not yet credited by the bank, ₦15,000;
(iii) bank charges of ₦2,500 shown only in the bank statement;
(iv) a standing order for insurance of ₦6,000 paid by the bank;
(v) a dividend of ₦9,000 paid directly into the account by a company;
(vi) a customer's cheque for ₦7,500 returned by the bank marked 'refer to drawer'.
